{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming to build up solutions for substrings.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of increasing length\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, add 2 to the LPS of the inner substring\n                if length == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum of excluding s[i] or s[j]\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
