{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Processes the input integer by converting it to a string, counting digit frequencies, and then checking constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _count_digit_frequencies(num_str: str) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Counts the frequency of each digit in a string representation of an integer.\"\"\"\n        frequencies = {}\n        for char_digit in num_str:\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            frequencies[digit] = frequencies.get(digit, 0) + 1\n        return frequencies\n\n    def _check_frequency_constraints(frequencies: dict) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if all digit frequencies satisfy the condition: count <= digit value.\"\"\"\n        for digit, count in frequencies.items():\n            if count > digit:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    num_str = str(num)\n    frequencies = _count_digit_frequencies(num_str)\n    return _check_frequency_constraints(frequencies)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array, k, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in a modified array which is formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    The 'target' parameter is unused as per the design context.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0\n\n    # Kadane's algorithm for a single array\n    def kadane_algorithm(arr):\n        max_so_far = float('-inf')\n        current_max = 0\n        for x in arr:\n            current_max += x\n            if current_max > max_so_far:\n                max_so_far = current_max\n            if current_max < 0:\n                current_max = 0\n        \n        # Handle case where all numbers are negative\n        if max_so_far == 0: # This happens if all current_max values reset to 0\n            return max(arr) # Return the largest single element\n        elif max_so_far == float('-inf'): # This happens if array is empty or other edge cases\n            return 0 # Or a more appropriate default based on problem context\n        return max_so_far\n\n    # Calculate max subarray sum for the original array (k=1)\n    max_single_array_sum = kadane_algorithm(array)\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_single_array_sum\n\n    array_sum = sum(array)\n\n    # Case 1: Max subarray is entirely within one repetition (already covered by max_single_array_sum)\n    # Case 2: Max subarray spans across two repetitions\n    # To handle this, consider an array formed by concatenating array with itself once: array + array\n    max_double_array_sum = kadane_algorithm(array + array)\n\n    if array_sum >= 0:\n        # If the sum of the original array is non-negative, and k > 1,\n        # the max sum can grow by adding (k-2) full repetitions of the array sum.\n        # It's either max_single_array_sum (if sum is negative) or max_double_array_sum potentially\n        # including the middle (k-2) blocks if array_sum is positive.\n        return max(max_single_array_sum, max_double_array_sum, array_sum * k) if k > 1 else max_single_array_sum\n    else: # array_sum < 0\n        # If the total sum of the array is negative, repeating it multiple times will only decrease the sum.\n        # So, the maximum subarray sum will be either within one block or at most span two blocks.\n        return max(max_single_array_sum, max_double_array_sum)"}
