{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost unset bit in the binary representation of the given integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Iterate from the highest possible bit position down to 0 to find the first unset bit.\n    # n.bit_length() determines the number of bits currently representing n.\n    for i in range(n.bit_length() - 1, -1, -1):\n        # If the current bit is 0, set it and return the modified number.\n        if not ((n >> i) & 1):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n\n    # If all existing bits are set, the leftmost unset bit is at the next highest position.\n    # Set this bit and return the result.\n    return n | (1 << n.bit_length())"}
