{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    The Perrin sequence is defined by P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3) with P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    perrin_numbers = []\n\n    # Initialize the first three Perrin numbers based on n's value\n    if n >= 0:\n        perrin_numbers.append(3)  # P(0)\n    if n >= 1:\n        perrin_numbers.append(0)  # P(1)\n    if n >= 2:\n        perrin_numbers.append(2)  # P(2)\n    \n    # Generate subsequent Perrin numbers up to P(n) using the recurrence relation\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        p_val = perrin_numbers[i-2] + perrin_numbers[i-3]\n        perrin_numbers.append(p_val)\n\n    # Calculate the sum of all generated Perrin numbers\n    return sum(perrin_numbers)"}
